public class CaseSurveyJob implements Queueable {
    private List<Id> caseIds;

    public CaseSurveyJob(List<Id> caseIds) {
        this.caseIds = caseIds;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        // Re-query in bulk to avoid stale trigger data
        Map<Id, Case> casesMap = new Map<Id, Case>([
            SELECT Id, CaseNumber, ContactId, IsClosed
            FROM Case
            WHERE Id IN :caseIds
        ]);

        List<Task> tasks = new List<Task>();
        for (Id cId : caseIds) {
            Case c = casesMap.get(cId);
            if (c == null) continue;

            // Final guard – case must still be closed and have a contact
            if (c.IsClosed && c.ContactId != null) {
                Task t = new Task();
                t.WhatId = c.Id;
                t.WhoId = c.ContactId;
                t.Subject = 'CSAT survey: ' + c.CaseNumber;
                t.ActivityDate = Date.today().addDays(2);
                t.Status = 'Not Started';
                tasks.add(t);
            }
        }

        if (!tasks.isEmpty()) {
            insert tasks;
        }
    }
}
```

Changes explained
* The trigger now collects all newly closed cases with a ContactId and enqueues a single Queueable per transaction instead of one job per case. The 50 queueable-jobs-per-transaction governor limit is hit with bulk closes (200 cases via API/list view). A single job preserves bulk safety and isolation – each case is built individually and the final insert is bulked.
* ContactId is checked in the trigger to avoid unnecessary jobs and in the job as a final guard.
* The Queueable now queries all cases in one SOQL and builds tasks in bulk, removing the per-case query and DML from the original version.

